index d395b59..1678106 100644
--- a/docs/billing.md
+++ b/docs/billing.md
@@ -35,6 +35,17 @@ Paused, canceled and past_due subscriptions are not renewed. Retrying past_due s
   - If `next_charge_at` passed while paused, the plan price is charged immediately (the "catch-up charge"), and `next_charge_at` moves past now with `advancePast`. If the catch-up charge fails, the subscription stays paused and the API answers `402`.
 - Every resume writes exactly one `subscription.resumed` event.
 
+## Concurrent requests
+
+Status changes are compare-and-set writes (`updateSubscriptionIf` in `src/repositories/subscriptions.ts`): the update only applies if the row still has the status the request read. A request that loses a race gets `409` and writes no event.
+
+Operations that await the gateway (the resume catch-up charge and each renewal) first take an operation lock on the row (`acquireLock`, columns `lock_token` / `locked_at`, migration `004_subscription_locks`). While it is held:
+
+- a second resume, a pause or a cancel answers `409 operation_in_progress` (the client retries);
+- the renewal job skips that subscription until its next run.
+
+So two overlapping resumes charge once and write one `subscription.resumed` event, and a cancel can never be overwritten by an in-flight resume or renewal. The lock expires after `LOCK_TTL_MS` (5 minutes) so a crashed process cannot block a subscription forever; if a gateway call outlives the lock and the subscription changed meanwhile, the charge is still recorded and the request answers `409 concurrent_change` for manual review.
+
 ## Cancel
 
 Cancel is immediate and terminal: `status = canceled`, `canceled_at` is now and `next_charge_at` becomes `null`. There are no refunds on cancel.
